  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 9. Preferred brackets: both ladders, insertions $1$ and $e^{2\\pi iu/h}$\nThis is Paul's choice, preferred for future work. Both brackets are residue sums over **all** poles of $\\rho$:\n$$\\langle f\\rangle_1=\\sum_{\\rm all\\ poles}\\mathrm{Res}\\,\\rho f,\\qquad \\langle f\\rangle_2=\\sum_{\\rm all\\ poles}\\mathrm{Res}\\,\\rho f\\,e^{2\\pi iu/h}.$$\nOn the pole $u=\\theta_s-nh$ the insertion equals $\\varepsilon_s=e^{2\\pi i\\theta_s/h}$. So $\\langle\\cdot\\rangle_1=\\langle\\cdot\\rangle_{\\theta_1}+\\langle\\cdot\\rangle_{\\theta_2}$ and $\\langle\\cdot\\rangle_2=\\varepsilon_1\\langle\\cdot\\rangle_{\\theta_1}+\\varepsilon_2\\langle\\cdot\\rangle_{\\theta_2}$, and the rows are the Section 7 rows mixed by $\\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\\\\\varepsilon_1&\\varepsilon_2\\end{pmatrix}$. The expectation is that only $c_0$ changes, by $(\\varepsilon_2-\\varepsilon_1)^3$. Below, everything is recomputed directly with the insertion; nothing is converted from Section 7.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ins[1][x_] := 1; ins[2][x_] := Exp[2 Pi I x/hN];\n(* bracket k: all poles, insertion ins[k] evaluated at the pole *)\nrowFb[B_, A_, {i_, j_}, k_] := Sum[N[wgt[p] ins[k][xP[p]], prec] With[{x = xP[p]}, {-QU[B, j, x] QD[A, i, x], -x QU[B, j, x] QD[A, i, x], QU[B, j, x] QD[A, i, x + hN], x QU[B, j, x] QD[A, i, x + hN], QU[B, j, x - hN] QD[A, i, x], x QU[B, j, x - hN] QD[A, i, x]}], {p, poles}];\nM18b[B_, A_] := Flatten[Table[rowFb[B, A, ij, k], {k, 2}, {ij, pairs9}], 1];\nsv18b = Table[svr[M18b[B, A]], {A, nS}, {B, nS}];\nchecks[\"insertion brackets: orthogonality max σmin/σmax, A≠B\"] = Max[Table[If[A != B, sv18b[[A, B]], 0], {A, nS}, {B, nS}]];\nchecks[\"insertion brackets: min σmin/σmax, A=B (not a zero test)\"] = Min[Diagonal[sv18b]];\ndetNb[B_, A_] := Det[Flatten[Table[rowFb[B, A, ij, k], {k, 2}, {ij, prsL1}], 1]];\ndVb = Table[detNb[B, \"vac\"], {B, nS}];\n(* c0 for these brackets, symbolically: εs = e^{2πiθ_s/h} kept as symbols; symbols outside the (x0,y0) monomials are zeroed BEFORE Det (same coefficients, much faster) *)\ninsS[1][s_] := 1; insS[2][s_] := ε[s];\nrowSb[{i_, j_}, k_] := Sum[wgtS[p] insS[k][p[[1]]] With[{x = xPs[p], s = p[[1]], n = p[[2]]}, {-Us[j, s, -n] Ds[i, s, -n], -x Us[j, s, -n] Ds[i, s, -n], Us[j, s, -n] Ds[i, s, -n + 1], x Us[j, s, -n] Ds[i, s, -n + 1], Us[j, s, -n - 1] Ds[i, s, -n], x Us[j, s, -n - 1] Ds[i, s, -n]}], {p, poles}];\ndetSymB = Expand[Det[Flatten[Table[rowSb[ij, k], {k, 2}, {ij, prsL1}], 1] /. (v : (Us | Ds)[__] /; ! MemberQ[keepVars, v]) -> 0]];\nc0Blist = Table[Factor[Together[Coefficient[detSymB, m/(m /. (Us | Ds)[__] -> 1)]/(m /. (Us | Ds)[__] -> 1)]], {m, monos}];\nc0B = First[c0Blist];\nchecks[\"insertion brackets: c0 same on all 16 monomials\"] = Union[Simplify[c0Blist - c0B]] === {0};\nchecks[\"insertion brackets: c0 = (ε2-ε1)^3 × per-ladder c0\"] = Simplify[c0B - (ε[2] - ε[1])^3 c0S] === 0;\nc0BN = N[c0B /. {ϑ1 -> thN[[1]], ϑ2 -> thN[[2]], ħ -> hN, ε[s_] :> Exp[2 Pi I thN[[s]]/hN]}, prec];\nRpredB = (Ω2 . y02)/(c0BN (Times @@ x0y0s) phiQvac);\nchecks[\"insertion brackets: full formula, max |lhs/rhs - 1| (all 64)\"] = Max[Abs[Table[ovl[[B]]/(RpredB x0ovl[[B]] dVb[[B]]/psiQ[B]), {B, nS}] - 1]];\nGrid[{{\"orthogonality A≠B\", ScientificForm[N[checks[\"insertion brackets: orthogonality max σmin/σmax, A≠B\"], 3], 3]}, {\"A=B (not zero)\", ScientificForm[N[checks[\"insertion brackets: min σmin/σmax, A=B (not a zero test)\"], 3], 3]}, {\"c0\", c0B}, {\"c0 same on 16 monomials\", checks[\"insertion brackets: c0 same on all 16 monomials\"]}, {\"c0 = (ε2-ε1)^3 c0(per-ladder)\", checks[\"insertion brackets: c0 = (ε2-ε1)^3 × per-ladder c0\"]}, {\"full formula, all 64\", ScientificForm[N[checks[\"insertion brackets: full formula, max |lhs/rhs - 1| (all 64)\"], 3], 3]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
