  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (exact, same numeric point).**\n- $\\langle v_{(1,1)}|R^{-1}$ is sparse: it has only 3 nonzero GT components, at weights $(2,1,0)$ (the highest weight), $(1,2,0)$ and one of the two $(1,1,1)$ states. $\\langle v_{(2,1)}|R^{-1}$ has all 8 components nonzero.\n- $R^{-1}$ moves into the auxiliary twist: $\\langle v_\\lambda|R^{-1}=e_1^T\\,T^{L=1,\\theta_1}_\\lambda\\big[g^{-T}\\mathrm{diag}(z)\\,g^{T}\\big](\\theta_1-2h)$ for both $\\lambda$, with $g=e^{r_1e_{12}}e^{r_2e_{13}}e^{r_3e_{23}}$ (fundamental). The twist $g^{-T}\\mathrm{diag}(z)g^T$ is lower-triangular-conjugated. This follows from the invariance of $\\mathcal L=u+h\\sum e_{ij}\\otimes E_{ij}$ under $g^{-T}\\otimes\\pi(g)$; the conjugations $gzg^{-1}$, $g^{-1}zg$ and $g^Tzg^{-T}$ all fail.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 10c. Projecting $\\langle v_\\lambda|R^{-1}\\otimes e_1^T$ onto the highest-weight spaces of $[2,1,0]^{\\otimes2}$\nFor each irrep $V_\\mu\\subset[2,1,0]\\otimes[2,1,0]$, the highest-weight space $\\mathrm{HW}_\\mu$ is the set of kets of total weight $\\mu$ that are killed by $E^{\\rm tot}_{12}$ and $E^{\\rm tot}_{23}$ (here $E^{\\rm tot}=E^{(1)}+E^{(2)}$). Its dimension is the multiplicity of $V_\\mu$. The covector $c_\\lambda=\\langle v_\\lambda|R^{-1}\\otimes e_1^T$ is projected onto $\\mathrm{HW}_\\mu$ with the invariant form; for the EH generators this is the plain dot product, since $EH^T_{ij}=EH_{ji}$. The table gives the overlaps $c_\\lambda\\cdot h^{(k)}_\\mu$ in an orthonormal basis of $\\mathrm{HW}_\\mu$, ordered by Gram–Schmidt, and the norm of the projection, which does not depend on the basis. The row $\\lambda=\\varnothing$ uses $c=e_1^T\\otimes e_1^T$ as a sanity check: it should reach only $[4,2,0]$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "Etot[i_, j_] := Etot[i, j] = E1[i, j] + E2[i, j];\n(* HW kets of weight μ: supported on that weight sector, killed by E12tot and E23tot *)\nhwBasis[μ_] := hwBasis[μ] = Module[{sec = Flatten[Position[wtBasis, μ]], ns},\n   ns = NullSpace[Join[Etot[1, 2][[All, sec]], Etot[2, 3][[All, sec]]]];\n   Simplify[Orthogonalize[Table[Normal[SparseArray[Thread[sec -> n], {d2}]], {n, ns}], Simplify[#1 . #2] &]]];\nirreps = Select[Union[wtBasis], Length[hwBasis[#]] > 0 &];\nchecks[\"decomposition: Σ mult · dim V_μ = 64\"] = Total[Length[hwBasis[#]] dim[#] & /@ irreps] == d2;\n(* covectors: λ = (1,1), (2,1), and ∅ (plain e1⊗e1) as a check *)\ncCov[\"11\"] = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[vR[\"11\"], UnitVector[d1, 1]]];\ncCov[\"21\"] = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[vR[\"21\"], UnitVector[d1, 1]]];\ncCov[\"∅\"] = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[UnitVector[d1, 1], UnitVector[d1, 1]]];\nhwOv[k_, μ_] := hwOv[k, μ] = RootReduce[cCov[k] . # & /@ hwBasis[μ]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"dim V_μ\", \"mult\", \"λ = ∅: overlaps\", \"λ = (1,1): overlaps\", \"|proj|\", \"λ = (2,1): overlaps\", \"|proj|\"}},\n   Table[{μ, dim[μ], Length[hwBasis[μ]], hwOv[\"∅\", μ], hwOv[\"11\", μ], RootReduce[Sqrt[Total[hwOv[\"11\", μ]^2]]], hwOv[\"21\", μ], RootReduce[Sqrt[Total[hwOv[\"21\", μ]^2]]]}, {μ, Reverse[irreps]}],\n   {{\"Σ mult·dim = 64\", checks[\"decomposition: Σ mult · dim V_μ = 64\"]}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
