  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (exact).** $[2,1,0]^{\\otimes2}=[4,2,0]\\oplus[4,1,1]\\oplus[3,3,0]\\oplus2\\,[3,2,1]\\oplus[2,2,2]$. Overlaps of $c_\\lambda$ with the orthonormal highest-weight kets:\n\n| $\\mu$ | $\\lambda=\\varnothing$ | $\\lambda=(1,1)$ | $\\lambda=(2,1)$ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| $[4,2,0]$ | $1$ | $5/8$ | $-5/24$ |\n| $[4,1,1]$ | $0$ | $0$ | $-2275/(8448\\sqrt2)$ |\n| $[3,3,0]$ | $0$ | $1/(10\\sqrt2)$ | $-1/(30\\sqrt2)$ |\n| $[3,2,1]$ (2 copies) | $(0,0)$ | $\\big(\\tfrac{7}{88}\\sqrt{7/3},\\,-\\tfrac{7}{176}\\sqrt{7/15}\\big)$ | $\\big(-\\tfrac{7}{176}\\sqrt{7/3},\\,\\tfrac{49}{2112}\\sqrt{7/15}\\big)$ |\n| $[2,2,2]$ | $0$ | $0$ | $343/(30976\\sqrt2)$ |\n\n- $(1,1)$ reaches $[4,2,0]$, $[3,3,0]$ and $[3,2,1]$, but not $[4,1,1]$ or the singlet. This fits its weight support: only the site-1 weights $(2,1,0)$, $(1,2,0)$ and $(1,1,1)$ occur.\n- $(2,1)$ reaches every irrep, including the singlet.\n- On the multiplicity-2 space $[3,2,1]$, the $(1,1)$ and $(2,1)$ projections are linearly independent, so together they reach both copies.\n- The $[3,2,1]$ coordinates depend on the Gram–Schmidt basis; whether they are zero and the rank do not.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 10d. Symbolic $z$, $w$, $h$\nThe site-1 vector $\\langle v_\\lambda|R^{-1}=\\langle\\Omega_{zw}|\\,T^{L=1,\\theta_1}_\\lambda(\\theta_1-2h)\\,R^{-1}$ involves only one-site $8\\times8$ objects. At $u=\\theta_1-2h$ the Lax depends only on $u-\\theta_1$, so $\\theta$ drops out, and the computation can be done with $z_i$, $w_i$ and $h$ symbolic. The rotation parameters $r_{1,2,3}(z,w)$ are those of Section 4. The localization on site 1 and the site-2 factor $f_\\lambda(\\theta_{12})$ come from Section 10 and are not re-derived here. The cell checks the symbolic result against the numeric point, then projects onto the highest-weight spaces of 10c.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "hS = ħh;\nrOmS = {r1 -> (w[1] - z[1])/(w[1] - z[2]), r2 -> ((w[1] - z[1]) (-w[2] + z[1]) (z[2] - z[3]))/((z[1] - z[2]) (w[1] - z[3]) (w[2] - z[3])), r3 -> ((w[1] - z[2]) (-w[2] + z[2]) (z[1] - z[3]))/((z[1] - z[2]) (w[1] - z[3]) (-w[2] + z[3]))};\nchecks[\"symbolic r's reproduce Section 4 at the numeric point\"] = ((({r1, r2, r3} /. rOmS) /. numZW) === ({r1, r2, r3} /. rOm));\n(* E_12, E_13, E_23 are nilpotent: exp is a finite sum. Start from the identity: MatrixPower[singular, 0] errors *)\nnexp[A_] := IdentityMatrix[Length[A]] + Sum[MatrixPower[A, k]/k!, {k, 1, 4}];\nRS = nexp[(r1 /. rOmS) Ee[1, 2]] . nexp[(r2 /. rOmS) Ee[1, 3]] . nexp[(r3 /. rOmS) Ee[2, 3]];\nRSinv = nexp[-(r3 /. rOmS) Ee[2, 3]] . nexp[-(r2 /. rOmS) Ee[1, 3]] . nexp[-(r1 /. rOmS) Ee[1, 2]];\nΩ1S = UnitVector[d1, 1] . RS;\n(* one-site T at shift δ = u - θ1, twist diag(z) on the right *)\nTS[δ_] := Table[(KroneckerDelta[i, k] δ IdentityMatrix[d1] + hS Ee[i, k]) z[k], {i, 3}, {k, 3}];\ntS[a_, δ_] := Sum[Sum[Signature[σ] Dot @@ Table[TS[δ - (k - 1) hS][[σ[[k]], I[[k]]]], {k, a}], {σ, Permutations[I]}], {I, Subsets[Range[3], {a}]}];\n(* u = θ1 - 2h  <=>  δ = -2h; T_(2,1)(u) = t2(u) t1(u+h) - t3(u+h) *)\nvRS[\"11\"] = Factor[Together[(Ω1S . tS[2, -2 hS]) . RSinv]];\nvRS[\"21\"] = Factor[Together[((Ω1S . tS[2, -2 hS]) . tS[1, -hS] - Ω1S . tS[3, -hS]) . RSinv]];\nnumPt = Join[numZW, {ħh -> hN}];\nchecks[\"symbolic <v_(1,1)|R^-1 = numeric at the point\"] = zeroQ[(vRS[\"11\"] /. numPt) - vR[\"11\"]];\nchecks[\"symbolic <v_(2,1)|R^-1 = numeric at the point\"] = zeroQ[(vRS[\"21\"] /. numPt) - vR[\"21\"]];\n(* the twist-conjugation identity, symbolically: <v|R^-1 = e1^T T_λ[g^-T z g^T](θ1-2h) *)\ngS = nexp[(r1 /. rOmS) ee[1, 2]] . nexp[(r2 /. rOmS) ee[1, 3]] . nexp[(r3 /. rOmS) ee[2, 3]];\nZt = Inverse[Transpose[gS]] . DiagonalMatrix[zs] . Transpose[gS];\nTSM[δ_] := Table[Sum[(KroneckerDelta[i, l] δ IdentityMatrix[d1] + hS Ee[i, l]) Zt[[l, k]], {l, 3}], {i, 3}, {k, 3}];\ntSM[a_, δ_] := Sum[Sum[Signature[σ] Dot @@ Table[TSM[δ - (k - 1) hS][[σ[[k]], I[[k]]]], {k, a}], {σ, Permutations[I]}], {I, Subsets[Range[3], {a}]}];\nchecks[\"symbolic: <v_(1,1)|R^-1 = e1^T T_(1,1)[g^-T z g^T]\"] = zeroQ[Together[vRS[\"11\"] - UnitVector[d1, 1] . tSM[2, -2 hS]]];\nchecks[\"symbolic: <v_(2,1)|R^-1 = e1^T T_(2,1)[g^-T z g^T]\"] = zeroQ[Together[vRS[\"21\"] - (UnitVector[d1, 1] . tSM[2, -2 hS] . tSM[1, -hS] - UnitVector[d1, 1] . tSM[3, -hS])]];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{k, checks[k]}, {k, {\"symbolic r's reproduce Section 4 at the numeric point\", \"symbolic <v_(1,1)|R^-1 = numeric at the point\", \"symbolic <v_(2,1)|R^-1 = numeric at the point\", \"symbolic: <v_(1,1)|R^-1 = e1^T T_(1,1)[g^-T z g^T]\", \"symbolic: <v_(2,1)|R^-1 = e1^T T_(2,1)[g^-T z g^T]\"}}], {\"check\", \"value\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
