  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (symbolic in $z$, $w$, $h$; exact).** All checks pass: agreement with the numeric point and with the twist-conjugation identity. The overlaps of $\\langle v_\\lambda|R^{-1}\\otimes e_1^T$ with the orthonormal HW kets are below. The full L=2 covector is $f_\\lambda(\\theta_{12})$ times this, with $f_\\lambda$ from Section 10 (fitted at one point). Write $z_{ij}=z_i-z_j$.\n\n| $\\mu$ | $\\lambda=(1,1)$ | $\\lambda=(2,1)$ |\n|---|---|---|\n| $[4,2,0]$ | $3h^2z_2z_3$ | $-3h^3z_2z_3^2$ |\n| $[4,1,1]$ | $0$ | $-\\dfrac{3h^3z_2z_3(z_2-w_1)(z_2-w_2)z_{13}z_{23}}{\\sqrt2\\,z_{12}(w_1-z_3)(w_2-z_3)}$ |\n| $[3,3,0]$ | $\\dfrac{3h^2(w_1-z_1)z_{12}z_3}{\\sqrt2(w_1-z_2)}$ | $-\\dfrac{3h^3(w_1-z_1)z_{12}z_3^2}{\\sqrt2(w_1-z_2)}$ |\n| $[3,2,1]_1$ | $2\\sqrt{3/7}\\,h^2X$ | $-3\\sqrt{3/7}\\,h^3z_3X$ |\n| $[3,2,1]_2$ | $-\\sqrt{3/35}\\,h^2X$ | $-\\sqrt{3/35}\\,h^3(2w_2-7z_2)\\,z_3X/w_2$ |\n| $[2,2,2]$ | $0$ | $\\dfrac{3h^3w_2(w_1-z_1)^2z_{13}^2z_{23}^2}{2\\sqrt2(w_1-z_3)^2(w_2-z_3)^2}$ |\n\nHere $X=\\dfrac{w_2(w_1-z_1)z_{13}z_{23}}{(w_1-z_3)(w_2-z_3)}$.\n- **(1,1).** The $[3,2,1]$ direction, $(2\\sqrt{3/7},-\\sqrt{3/35})$, does not depend on $z$ or $w$: it is the image of $e_5^T\\otimes e_1^T$.\n- **(2,1).** Its $[3,2,1]$ direction does depend on $z_2/w_2$.\n- **Relation between the two.** On $[4,2,0]$ and $[3,3,0]$, the $(2,1)$ overlap is $-hz_3$ times the $(1,1)$ overlap.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 10e. Small-twist limit $z_k=e^{\\varepsilon\\phi_k}$, $w_k=e^{\\varepsilon\\omega_k}$\nEach HW overlap from 10d is expanded in $\\varepsilon\\to0$ with generic $\\phi_k$ and $\\omega_k$. The cell reports the leading power $\\varepsilon^{\\#}$ and its coefficient. For $[3,2,1]$, $\\#$ is the lowest order of the 2-vector, which does not depend on the HW basis.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "epsSub = Join[Table[z[k] -> Exp[ε φ[k]], {k, 3}], Table[w[k] -> Exp[ε ω[k]], {k, 3}]];\n(* leading term of a list of overlaps: lowest power of ε among the components, and the coefficient vector there *)\nleadEps[expr_List] := Module[{ser = Normal[Series[expr /. epsSub, {ε, 0, 5}]], n},\n   If[AllTrue[Flatten[{expr}], # === 0 &], {\"∞ (vanishes)\", 0},\n    n = Min[Table[If[Simplify[e] === 0, Infinity, Exponent[e, ε, Min]], {e, Expand[ser]}]];\n    {n, Factor[Simplify[Coefficient[Expand[ser], ε, n]]]}]];\nepsTab = Table[{μ, leadEps[hwOvS[\"11\", μ]], leadEps[hwOvS[\"21\", μ]]}, {μ, Reverse[irreps]}];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"(1,1): #\", \"(1,1): leading coeff\", \"(2,1): #\", \"(2,1): leading coeff\"}}, Table[{r[[1]], r[[2, 1]], r[[2, 2]], r[[3, 1]], r[[3, 2]]}, {r, epsTab}]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
