  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result.** Leading order of the HW overlaps of $\\langle v_\\lambda|R^{-1}\\otimes e_1^T$ as $\\varepsilon\\to0$, with $\\phi_{ij}=\\phi_i-\\phi_j$:\n\n| $\\mu$ | $(1,1)$: $\\#$ | $(2,1)$: $\\#$ |\n|---|---|---|\n| $[4,2,0]$ | 0 | 0 |\n| $[4,1,1]$ | (exactly 0) | 1 |\n| $[3,3,0]$ | 1 | 1 |\n| $[3,2,1]$ (both components) | 1 | 1 |\n| $[2,2,2]$ | (exactly 0) | 2 |\n\nThe leading coefficients are the 10d formulas with $z_i-z_j\\to\\varepsilon\\phi_{ij}$ and $w_i-z_j\\to\\varepsilon(\\omega_i-\\phi_j)$, and with $z,w\\to1$ elsewhere. For example, the $(2,1)$ singlet is $\\varepsilon^2\\cdot3h^3\\phi_{13}^2\\phi_{23}^2(\\phi_1-\\omega_1)^2/[2\\sqrt2(\\phi_3-\\omega_1)^2(\\phi_3-\\omega_2)^2]$. On $[3,2,1]$ the leading directions are $(2\\sqrt{3/7},-\\sqrt{3/35})$ for $(1,1)$ and $(-3\\sqrt{3/7},\\sqrt{15/7})$ for $(2,1)$. These stay independent at $\\varepsilon^1$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 10f. Do the leading-$\\varepsilon$ vectors span each weight sector of $e_j^T\\otimes e_1^T$?\nThe covectors $e_j^T\\otimes e_1^T$ ($j=1..8$) have 7 distinct total weights, $\\mathrm{wt}_j+(2,1,0)$. Every sector is 1-dimensional except total weight $(3,2,1)$, which is 2-dimensional (site-1 GT states 4 and 5). For each sector, take the restriction of $\\langle v_\\lambda|R^{-1}$ to that sector with $z_k=e^{\\varepsilon\\phi_k}$, $w_k=e^{\\varepsilon\\omega_k}$, and find its leading order $\\varepsilon^{\\#}$ and coefficient vector. The vectors are collected over $\\lambda\\in\\{(1,1),(2,1)\\}$ and 8 random rational $\\omega$'s, with generic $\\phi=(1/3,-2/7,5/11)$ and $h=1$. The question is whether their rank equals the dimension of the sector. On the dominant sectors this is the HW-multiplicity question of 10c–10e, since the multiplicities are 1, 1, 1, 2, 1.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* site-1 weight sectors (site 2 is e1, weight (2,1,0)) *)\nsecs1 = GatherBy[Range[d1], wts[[#]] &];\nφN = {1/3, -2/7, 5/11}; tol = 10^-9;\nSeedRandom[7]; ωSamples = Table[RandomInteger[{-40, 40}, 3]/RandomChoice[{7, 9, 11, 13}], 8];\nClearAll[epsCoefs];\n(* ε-series coefficients n = 0..4 of the site-1 vector (exact, then numeric) *)\nepsCoefs[k_, ωv_] := epsCoefs[k, ωv] = Module[{a = vRS[k] /. ħh -> 1 /. Join[Table[z[i] -> Exp[ε φN[[i]]], {i, 3}], Table[w[i] -> Exp[ε ωv[[i]]], {i, 3}]]},\n   Table[N[SeriesCoefficient[#, {ε, 0, n}] & /@ a], {n, 0, 4}]];\nleadSec[k_, ωv_, sec_] := Module[{cs = epsCoefs[k, ωv][[All, sec]], n},\n   n = SelectFirst[Range[0, 4], Max[Abs[cs[[# + 1]]]] > tol &, Missing[]];\n   If[MissingQ[n], {∞, None}, {n, cs[[n + 1]]}]];\nrankN[M_] := If[M === {} || Max[Abs[Flatten[M]]] < tol, 0, With[{sv = SingularValueList[N[M], Tolerance -> 0]}, Count[sv, x_ /; x > tol Max[sv]]]];\nsecTab = Table[With[{L11 = Table[leadSec[\"11\", ωv, sec], {ωv, ωSamples}], L21 = Table[leadSec[\"21\", ωv, sec], {ωv, ωSamples}]},\n    {wts[[sec[[1]]]] + {2, 1, 0}, sec, Length[sec], Union[L11[[All, 1]]], Union[L21[[All, 1]]],\n     rankN[DeleteCases[L11[[All, 2]], None]], rankN[DeleteCases[L21[[All, 2]], None]], rankN[DeleteCases[Join[L11[[All, 2]], L21[[All, 2]]], None]]}], {sec, secs1}];\nchecks[\"leading-ε vectors span every weight sector of e_j⊗e_1\"] = AllTrue[secTab, #[[8]] == #[[3]] &];\nGrid[Join[{{\"total weight\", \"site-1 GT states\", \"dim\", \"# (1,1)\", \"# (2,1)\", \"rank (1,1)\", \"rank (2,1)\", \"rank both\"}}, secTab,\n   {{\"all sectors spanned\", checks[\"leading-ε vectors span every weight sector of e_j⊗e_1\"]}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
