  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result** ($\\phi=(1/3,-2/7,5/11)$, $h=1$, 8 random $\\omega$'s): **yes, every weight sector is spanned** at leading order once both $\\lambda$'s are used.\n\n| total weight | site-1 GT | dim | $\\#$ (1,1) | $\\#$ (2,1) | rank (1,1) | rank (2,1) | rank both |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| $(4,2,0)$ | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 1 |\n| $(4,1,1)$ | 2 | 1 | — | 1 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n| $(3,3,0)$ | 3 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 |\n| $(3,2,1)$ | 4, 5 | 2 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | **2** |\n| $(3,1,2)$ | 6 | 1 | — | 2 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n| $(2,3,1)$ | 7 | 1 | — | 2 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n| $(2,2,2)$ | 8 | 1 | — | 2 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n\n- **Sector $(3,2,1)$.** Varying $\\omega$ never adds a direction. At order $\\varepsilon$, (1,1) gives $(0,1)$ in $(e_4,e_5)$ and (2,1) gives the fixed direction $\\propto(-1/\\sqrt2,\\sqrt{3/2})$. Only together do they make rank 2.\n- **Other sectors.** (1,1) is exactly zero on GT states 2, 4, 6, 7 and 8, so (2,1) alone covers those sectors. The orders agree with counting the factors $z_i-z_j$ and $w_i-z_j$ in the 10d entries.\n- **Relation to 10c–10e.** On the dominant weights this is the HW-multiplicity statement, with multiplicities 1, 1, 1, 2, 1.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* HW states are fixed by their e_j⊗e_1 components: restricting HW_μ to the slots (j,1) is injective (rank = multiplicity) *)\nslots1 = Table[(j - 1) d1 + 1, {j, d1}];\ninjTab = Table[{μ, Length[hwBasis[μ]], MatrixRank[N[hwBasis[μ][[All, slots1]], 30]]}, {μ, Reverse[irreps]}];\nchecks[\"HW_μ → (e_j⊗e_1 components) injective for all μ\"] = AllTrue[injTab, #[[2]] == #[[3]] &];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"mult\", \"rank on e_j⊗e_1 slots\"}}, injTab, {{\"injective\", checks[\"HW_μ → (e_j⊗e_1 components) injective for all μ\"]}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
