  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (11c).** Orders $\\#$ (ratio of $\\varepsilon=10^{-9}$ and $10^{-6}$; $\\phi=(1/3,-2/7,5/11)$, $\\omega=(2/5,1/7,-3/4)$, main chain point):\n\n| $\\mu$ | $c_{11}\\!\\cdot\\!RR\\Psi$ | $c_{11}\\!\\cdot\\!P_{HW}\\Psi$ | $c_{21}\\!\\cdot\\!RR\\Psi$ | $c_{21}\\!\\cdot\\!P_{HW}\\Psi$ | $T_\\lambda$ | $\\langle\\Omega|\\hat\\Psi\\rangle$ | $\\langle x_0|\\hat\\Psi\\rangle$ | $\\langle x_0|P_{HW}\\hat\\Psi\\rangle$ |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [4,2,0] | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 2 | 2 |\n| [4,1,1] | **1** | **exact 0** | 1 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 3 | exact 0 |\n| [3,3,0] | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 3 | exact 0 |\n| [3,2,1]± | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 4 | exact 0 |\n| [2,2,2] | **2** | **exact 0** | 2 | 2 | 0 | 2 | 6 | exact 0 |\n\n- **The identity holds exactly** at small twist ($|L_2/L_3-1|=0$ to 160 digits), so $f_\\lambda$ also holds at these new $z,w$.\n- **$x_0$ and $\\Omega$ are both coherent states in $[4,2,0]^*$.** Each is $(e_1^T\\pi(g))^{\\otimes2}$, so it annihilates every other irrep and only sees $P_{27}\\Psi_B$; hence $\\langle x_0|P_{HW}\\Psi\\rangle=0$ exactly for $\\mu\\ne[4,2,0]$. All the Q-formula ratio contains is the ratio of two overlaps with the 27-admixture of the twisted eigenstate, which is $O(\\varepsilon^{\\rm ht})$.\n- **Replacing $(R\\otimes R)\\Psi_B$ by its HW limit is not valid at leading order** (except for $[4,2,0]$). $(R\\otimes R)$ acts nontrivially on the $O(\\varepsilon)$ admixture of other irreps' descendants, and that contributes at the same order as $c_\\lambda\\cdot P_{HW}\\Psi$:\n  - For $(1,1)$ at $[4,1,1]$ and $[2,2,2]$ the CG overlap is exactly 0, but the chain gives $\\varepsilon^1$, $\\varepsilon^2$.\n  - Otherwise the orders agree, but $c_\\lambda\\cdot(R\\otimes R)\\hat\\Psi\\big/c_\\lambda\\cdot P_{HW}\\hat\\Psi\\to\\kappa_{B,\\lambda}\\ne1$.\n- **$\\kappa_{B,\\lambda}$ is independent of $\\phi$ and $\\omega$** (3 twist directions, agreement to $\\sim10^{-9}$). It is untwisted data. With $t=\\theta_{12}/h$:\n  - $[3,3,0]$ (both $\\lambda$) and $[4,1,1]$ $(2,1)$: $\\kappa=(t+1)/2$. That is 97/70 at $t=62/35$ and 22/15 at $t=29/15$, so validated at a second point.\n  - $[2,2,2]$ $(2,1)$: $\\kappa=(t+1)(t+3)/12$, **pair-fitted** on the two points.\n  - $[3,2,1]$ copies: (1.5294, 1.0723) and (0.6420, 0.7717) at $t=62/35$, presumably involving $\\sqrt{4+5t^2}$; not identified.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 11d. Weight-by-weight decomposition of the chain, with $\\langle x_0|\\Psi_B\\rangle=1$\nNormalize $\\Psi_B$ by $\\langle x_0|\\Psi_B\\rangle=1$, so that $\\Psi_B=\\varepsilon^{-k}(h_\\mu+O(\\varepsilon))$. $\\Psi_B$ has exact total weight $\\mu$ and $R$ contains only raising operators, so\n$$c_\\lambda\\cdot(R\\otimes R)\\Psi_B=\\sum_{\\nu\\ge\\mu}c^{(\\nu)}_\\lambda\\cdot\\big[(R\\otimes R)\\Psi_B\\big]_\\nu ,$$\nwhere $c^{(\\nu)}_\\lambda$ is the weight-$\\nu$ part of $c_\\lambda=\\langle v_\\lambda|R^{-1}\\otimes e_1^T$.\n- **$\\nu=\\mu$:** the term $c^{(\\mu)}_\\lambda\\cdot\\Psi_B\\to\\varepsilon^{-k}c^{(\\mu)}_\\lambda\\cdot h_\\mu$, the CG data of 10c–10e.\n- **$\\nu>\\mu$:** these terms vanish on $h_\\mu$, so $[(R\\otimes R)\\Psi_B]_\\nu=O(\\varepsilon^{1-k})$. Their size relative to the $\\nu=\\mu$ term is set by $\\|c^{(\\nu)}_\\lambda\\|$ versus $\\|c^{(\\mu)}_\\lambda\\|$.\n\nThe table lists, for each HW-limit state and $\\lambda$, the $\\varepsilon$-order of every nonzero weight contribution, together with the orders of $\\|c^{(\\nu)}\\|$ and $\\|[(R\\otimes R)\\Psi]_\\nu\\|$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* per-weight pieces of c_λ·(R⊗R)Ψ with <x0|Ψ> = 1 *)\ncgParts[eps_, φv_, ωv_, pr_] := Module[{zE, wE, tt, mix, rr, Rg, RgI, Om1, RR, Pph, rsE, x02e, uLl = thN[[1]] - 2 hN, v11, v21, cl, out = {}},\n  zE = N[Exp[eps φv], pr]; wE = N[Exp[eps ωv], pr];\n  tt = Table[tPoly[DiagonalMatrix[zE], a], {a, 2}]; mix = (tt[[1]] + N[Pi, pr] tt[[2]]) /. u -> 3/7;\n  rr = rOmF[zE, wE];\n  Rg = nexpS[rr[[1]] EeN[1, 2]] . nexpS[rr[[2]] EeN[1, 3]] . nexpS[rr[[3]] EeN[2, 3]]; RgI = nexpS[-rr[[3]] EeN[2, 3]] . nexpS[-rr[[2]] EeN[1, 3]] . nexpS[-rr[[1]] EeN[1, 2]];\n  Om1 = UnitVector[d1, 1] . Rg; RR = KroneckerProduct[Rg, Rg];\n  rsE = rsSol /. Thread[zs -> zE];\n  Pph = nexpS[(r[1] /. rsE) Ee[3, 2]] . nexpS[(r[2] /. rsE) Ee[3, 1]] . nexpS[(r[3] /. rsE) Ee[2, 1]] . DiagonalMatrix[Table[Product[(s[k] /. rsE)^J0[k][p], {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Λ}]}]] . nexpS[(1/zE[[1]]) Ee[1, 2]] . nexpS[-(1/(zE[[1]] zE[[2]])) Ee[1, 3]] . nexpS[((zE[[1]] + zE[[2]])/(zE[[1]] zE[[2]])) Ee[2, 3]];\n  x02e = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[#, #]] &[UnitVector[d1, 1] . Inverse[Pph]];\n  v11 = Om1 . t1zE[2, uLl, zE]; v21 = v11 . t1zE[1, uLl + hN, zE] - Om1 . t1zE[3, uLl + hN, zE];\n  cl = {Flatten[KroneckerProduct[v11 . RgI, UnitVector[d1, 1]]], Flatten[KroneckerProduct[v21 . RgI, UnitVector[d1, 1]]]};\n  Do[With[{sec = Flatten[Position[wtBasis, Λw]]}, With[{es = Eigensystem[mix[[sec, sec]]]}, Do[With[{ψ0 = Normal[SparseArray[Thread[sec -> es[[2, k]]], {d2}]]}, If[(Norm[EtotS[1, 2] . ψ0] + Norm[EtotS[2, 3] . ψ0])/Norm[ψ0] < 10^-3,\n        With[{ψ = ψ0/(x02e . ψ0)}, With[{RRψ = RR . ψ},\n          AppendTo[out, <|\"mu\" -> Λw, \"ev\" -> es[[1, k]], \"normψ\" -> Norm[ψ], \"parts\" -> Table[{wtBasis[[sn[[1]]]], Table[cl[[l]][[sn]] . RRψ[[sn]], {l, 2}], Table[Norm[cl[[l]][[sn]]], {l, 2}], Norm[RRψ[[sn]]]}, {sn, sectors}]|>]]]]], {k, Length[sec]}]]], {Λw, hwSecs}];\n  SortBy[out, {Position[hwSecs, #[\"mu\"]][[1, 1]], Re[#[\"ev\"]]} &]];\ncpD = Table[cgParts[e, φT, ωT, 200], {e, epsC}];\nordP[a_, b_] := If[Abs[a] < 10^-150 || Abs[b] < 10^-150, \"0\", N[Round[Log[Abs[b/a]]/Log[epsC[[2]]/epsC[[1]]], 1/100]]];\n(* rows: state, λ, then for each total weight ν ≥ μ with a nonzero contribution: {ν, order of contribution, order of ||c^(ν)||, order of ||[RRΨ]_ν||} *)\npartTab = Flatten[Table[With[{A = cpD[[1, b]], B = cpD[[2, b]]}, {A[\"mu\"], l, N[ordP[A[\"normψ\"], B[\"normψ\"]]], Select[Table[With[{pa = A[\"parts\"][[j]], pb = B[\"parts\"][[j]]}, {pa[[1]], ordP[pa[[2, l]], pb[[2, l]]], ordP[pa[[3, l]], pb[[3, l]]], ordP[pa[[4]], pb[[4]]]}], {j, Length[sectors]}], #[[2]] =!= \"0\" &]}], {b, Length[cpD[[1]]]}, {l, 2}], 1];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"λ (1=(1,1), 2=(2,1))\", \"# ||Ψ|| (<x0|Ψ>=1)\", \"{ν, # contribution, # ||c^(ν)||, # ||[RRΨ]_ν||}\"}}, partTab], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
