  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (11d).** With $\\langle x_0|\\Psi_B\\rangle=1$, $\\|\\Psi_B\\|\\sim\\varepsilon^{-k}$ with $k=2,3,3,4,4,6$ for $[4,2,0],[4,1,1],[3,3,0],[3,2,1]_\\pm,[2,2,2]$. Contributions $c^{(\\nu)}_\\lambda\\cdot[(R\\otimes R)\\Psi_B]_\\nu$, listed as $\\nu$: order of the contribution $=$ order of $\\|c^{(\\nu)}\\|$ $+$ order of $\\|[RR\\Psi]_\\nu\\|$:\n- **[4,1,1], (2,1):** $\\nu=[4,1,1]$: $-2=1-3$; $\\nu=[4,2,0]$: $-2=0-2$. For (1,1) only $\\nu=[4,2,0]$ contributes ($c^{(411)}_{11}=0$).\n- **[3,3,0], both $\\lambda$:** $\\nu=[3,3,0]$: $-2=1-3$; $\\nu=[4,2,0]$: $-2=0-2$.\n- **[3,2,1]:** $\\nu=[3,2,1]$: $-3=1-4$; $\\nu=[4,2,0]$: $-3=0-3$; $\\nu=[3,3,0]$ and $[4,1,1]$: $-2=1-3$, which is subleading.\n- **[2,2,2], (2,1):** $\\nu=[2,2,2]$: $-4$; $\\nu=[4,2,0]$: $-4=0-4$; the rest are $-3$. For (1,1), $\\nu=[2,2,2]$ is absent ($c^{(222)}_{11}=0$) and $\\nu=[4,2,0],[3,2,1]$ give $-4$.\n\n**Mechanism.** $(R\\otimes R)\\Psi_B$ indeed keeps its leading piece $\\varepsilon^{-k}h_\\mu$, and its higher-weight pieces are suppressed. But $c_\\lambda$ is not uniform: $c^{(\\mu)}_\\lambda=O(\\varepsilon^{1\\text{ or }2})$ while $c^{(420)}_\\lambda=O(1)$. The large higher-weight components of $c_\\lambda$ pair with the subleading higher-weight pieces of $(R\\otimes R)\\Psi_B$, at the same order as the CG term. The $\\nu=\\mu$ term is exactly $c^{(\\mu)}_\\lambda\\cdot\\Psi_B$ (raising operators do not change the weight-$\\mu$ component), and its leading part $\\varepsilon^{-k}c^{(\\mu)}_\\lambda\\cdot h_\\mu$ is the 10e CG data. The Q side, $T^B_\\lambda\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi_B\\rangle/f_\\lambda$, gives only the sum over $\\nu$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 11e. The projected covector $W_\\mu=\\langle v_\\lambda\\otimes\\Omega_{zw}|P_\\mu$\n$W_\\mu\\cdot\\Psi_B$ is exactly the left-hand side (it equals $T^B_\\lambda\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi_B\\rangle/f_\\lambda$). Question: if $W_\\mu=\\varepsilon^{a}(w_0+O(\\varepsilon))$ and $\\Psi_B=\\varepsilon^{-k}(h_\\mu+O(\\varepsilon))$ with $\\langle x_0|\\Psi_B\\rangle=1$, is the leading term $\\varepsilon^{a-k}\\,w_0\\cdot h_\\mu$? The cell reports the orders of $\\|W_\\mu\\|$, of $W_\\mu\\cdot h_\\mu$ (the norm of the projection onto $\\mathrm{HW}_\\mu$ for the octet) and of $W_\\mu\\cdot\\Psi_B$, together with $|w_0\\cdot h_\\mu|/\\|w_0\\|$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "wData[eps_, φv_, ωv_, pr_] := Module[{zE, wE, tt, mix, rr, Rg, Om1, Pph, rsE, x02e, uLl = thN[[1]] - 2 hN, v11, v21, cov, out = {}},\n  zE = N[Exp[eps φv], pr]; wE = N[Exp[eps ωv], pr];\n  tt = Table[tPoly[DiagonalMatrix[zE], a], {a, 2}]; mix = (tt[[1]] + N[Pi, pr] tt[[2]]) /. u -> 3/7;\n  rr = rOmF[zE, wE]; Rg = nexpS[rr[[1]] EeN[1, 2]] . nexpS[rr[[2]] EeN[1, 3]] . nexpS[rr[[3]] EeN[2, 3]]; Om1 = UnitVector[d1, 1] . Rg;\n  rsE = rsSol /. Thread[zs -> zE];\n  Pph = nexpS[(r[1] /. rsE) Ee[3, 2]] . nexpS[(r[2] /. rsE) Ee[3, 1]] . nexpS[(r[3] /. rsE) Ee[2, 1]] . DiagonalMatrix[Table[Product[(s[k] /. rsE)^J0[k][p], {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Λ}]}]] . nexpS[(1/zE[[1]]) Ee[1, 2]] . nexpS[-(1/(zE[[1]] zE[[2]])) Ee[1, 3]] . nexpS[((zE[[1]] + zE[[2]])/(zE[[1]] zE[[2]])) Ee[2, 3]];\n  x02e = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[#, #]] &[UnitVector[d1, 1] . Inverse[Pph]];\n  v11 = Om1 . t1zE[2, uLl, zE]; v21 = v11 . t1zE[1, uLl + hN, zE] - Om1 . t1zE[3, uLl + hN, zE];\n  cov = {Flatten[KroneckerProduct[v11, Om1]], Flatten[KroneckerProduct[v21, Om1]]};\n  Do[With[{sec = Flatten[Position[wtBasis, Λw]], hb = hwB[Λw]}, With[{es = Eigensystem[mix[[sec, sec]]]}, Do[With[{ψ0 = Normal[SparseArray[Thread[sec -> es[[2, k]]], {d2}]]}, If[(Norm[EtotS[1, 2] . ψ0] + Norm[EtotS[2, 3] . ψ0])/Norm[ψ0] < 10^-3,\n        With[{ψ = ψ0/(x02e . ψ0)}, With[{W = Table[Normal[SparseArray[Thread[sec -> cov[[l]][[sec]]], {d2}]], {l, 2}]},\n          AppendTo[out, <|\"mu\" -> Λw, \"ev\" -> es[[1, k]], \"W\" -> W, \"normW\" -> Norm /@ W, \"Wh\" -> Table[Norm[hb . W[[l]]], {l, 2}], \"WΨ\" -> Table[W[[l]] . ψ, {l, 2}]|>]]]]], {k, Length[sec]}]]], {Λw, hwSecs}];\n  SortBy[out, {Position[hwSecs, #[\"mu\"]][[1, 1]], Re[#[\"ev\"]]} &]];\nwD = Table[wData[e, φT, ωT, 200], {e, epsC}];\nwTab = Flatten[Table[With[{A = wD[[1, b]], B = wD[[2, b]]}, {A[\"mu\"], {\"(1,1)\", \"(2,1)\"}[[l]], ordP[A[\"normW\"][[l]], B[\"normW\"][[l]]], ordP[A[\"Wh\"][[l]], B[\"Wh\"][[l]]], ordP[A[\"WΨ\"][[l]], B[\"WΨ\"][[l]]], If[A[\"mu\"] == {4, 2, 0}, 1, N[B[\"Wh\"][[l]]/B[\"normW\"][[l]], 3]]}], {b, Length[wD[[1]]]}, {l, 2}], 1];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"λ\", \"# ||W_μ||\", \"# W_μ·h_μ\", \"# W_μ·Ψ (<x0|Ψ>=1)\", \"|W·h|/||W|| at ε=1e-9\"}}, wTab], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
