   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (11g).** With $C=c_{(2,1)}+hz_3c_{(1,1)}$:\n- **$[4,1,1]$ and both $[3,2,1]$ copies: $\\kappa_C=1$** (to $10^{-10}=O(\\varepsilon)$) for 3 twist directions and at both chain points. The Q side then gives the HW CG data directly.\n- **$[4,2,0]$, $[3,3,0]$:** $C$ vanishes exactly on both sides. $[4,2,0]$ is clean with either $\\lambda$ alone ($\\kappa=1$). $[3,3,0]$ still needs another covector.\n- **$[2,2,2]$:** $\\kappa_C=97/105$ at $t=62/35$ and $44/45$ at $t=29/15$, i.e. $\\kappa_C=(t+1)/3$ (**pair-fitted**, one parameter, two points). The remaining contamination comes from the intermediate weights $[4,1,1],[3,3,0],[3,2,1]$. It is independent of $\\phi,\\omega$.\n- **Lesson.** Contamination is removable by choosing linear combinations of Q-computable insertions ($T_\\lambda$ at $\\theta_1-2h$, weighted by $z$) that kill the higher-weight components of the covector at the orders that matter.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 11h. Reconstruction from many $w$: rank of the localized covectors\nOnly $T_{(1,1)}$ and $T_{(2,1)}$ at $\\theta_1-2h$ are allowed, but the vacuum twist $w$ is free: the overlap formula holds for every $w$. The question is the rank, in each dominant weight sector $\\mu$, of $\\{\\langle v_\\lambda(w)\\otimes\\Omega_{zw}|P_\\mu\\}$ over $\\lambda$ and many $w$ (twist $z$ fixed), with and without the normalization row $\\langle x_0|P_\\mu$. Full rank means $\\Psi_B(\\varepsilon)$ is determined by Q data at each $\\varepsilon$. $\\Omega_{zw}$ depends only on $(w_1,w_2)$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "wCov[eps_, φv_, ωv_, pr_] := Module[{zE = N[Exp[eps φv], pr], wE = N[Exp[eps ωv], pr], rr, Om1, uLl = thN[[1]] - 2 hN, v11, v21},\n  rr = rOmF[zE, wE]; Om1 = UnitVector[d1, 1] . nexpS[rr[[1]] EeN[1, 2]] . nexpS[rr[[2]] EeN[1, 3]] . nexpS[rr[[3]] EeN[2, 3]];\n  v11 = Om1 . t1zE[2, uLl, zE]; v21 = v11 . t1zE[1, uLl + hN, zE] - Om1 . t1zE[3, uLl + hN, zE];\n  {Flatten[KroneckerProduct[v11, Om1]], Flatten[KroneckerProduct[v21, Om1]]}];\nx0Cov[eps_, φv_, pr_] := Module[{zE = N[Exp[eps φv], pr], rsE, Pph}, rsE = rsSol /. Thread[zs -> zE];\n  Pph = nexpS[(r[1] /. rsE) Ee[3, 2]] . nexpS[(r[2] /. rsE) Ee[3, 1]] . nexpS[(r[3] /. rsE) Ee[2, 1]] . DiagonalMatrix[Table[Product[(s[k] /. rsE)^J0[k][p], {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Λ}]}]] . nexpS[(1/zE[[1]]) Ee[1, 2]] . nexpS[-(1/(zE[[1]] zE[[2]])) Ee[1, 3]] . nexpS[((zE[[1]] + zE[[2]])/(zE[[1]] zE[[2]])) Ee[2, 3]];\n  Flatten[KroneckerProduct[#, #]] &[UnitVector[d1, 1] . Inverse[Pph]]];\nSeedRandom[5]; ωMany = Table[RandomInteger[{-40, 40}, 3]/RandomChoice[{7, 11, 13, 17}], 30];\nrankTol[m_, tol_] := With[{sv = SingularValueList[m, Tolerance -> 0]}, {Count[sv, x_ /; x > tol First[sv]], N[sv/First[sv], 3]}];\nrkTab = Table[With[{sec = Flatten[Position[wtBasis, μ]]}, With[{rows = Flatten[Table[wCov[1/3, φT, ωv, 80][[All, sec]], {ωv, ωMany}], 1], xr = x0Cov[1/3, φT, 80][[sec]]},\n     {μ, Length[sec], rankTol[rows, 10^-40][[1]], rankTol[Append[rows, xr], 10^-40][[1]]}]], {μ, hwSecs}];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"dim weight space\", \"rank {W_λ(w)}\", \"rank with x0\"}}, rkTab], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
