ine\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-16.9613em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:10.0806em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-18.1613em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:10.0806em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.5806em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[2321]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\varepsilon  & \\mu  & \\text{dim} & \\text{rank (with x0)} & \\text{1 - |cos| HW direction} & \\text{rel. error of HW part (incl. scale)}\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000} & \\left\\{4,2,0\\right\\} & 1 & 1 & 0.\\times 10^{-190} & 0\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000} & \\left\\{4,1,1\\right\\} & 2 & 2 & 0.\\times 10^{-177} & 0\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000} & \\left\\{3,3,0\\right\\} & 2 & 2 & 0.\\times 10^{-177} & 0\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000} & \\left\\{3,2,1\\right\\} & 6 & 5 & 0.0242 & 0.321\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000} & \\left\\{3,2,1\\right\\} & 6 & 5 & 0.0485 & 0.389\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000} & \\left\\{2,2,2\\right\\} & 10 & 7 & 0.\\times 10^{-145} & 0.0762\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000000} & \\left\\{4,2,0\\right\\} & 1 & 1 & 0.\\times 10^{-187} & 0\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000000} & \\left\\{4,1,1\\right\\} & 2 & 2 & 0.\\times 10^{-168} & 0\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000000} & \\left\\{3,3,0\\right\\} & 2 & 2 & 0.\\times 10^{-168} & 0\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000000} & \\left\\{3,2,1\\right\\} & 6 & 5 & 0.0242 & 0.321\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000000} & \\left\\{3,2,1\\right\\} & 6 & 5 & 0.0485 & 0.389\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000000} & \\left\\{2,2,2\\right\\} & 10 & 7 & 0.\\times 10^{-124} & 0.0762\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "38012b76-7f6c-46bb-ac3e-3b6bc7055f46"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (11h).** The data are all $w$ (20 random), both $\\lambda$, plus $\\langle x_0|\\Psi\\rangle=1$, and they determine $\\Psi_B(\\varepsilon)$ on its weight space up to the exact null space of the covector family. Rank, with $x_0$:\n- **$[4,2,0]$, $[4,1,1]$, $[3,3,0]$: full rank.** $\\Psi_B$ is reconstructed exactly at every $\\varepsilon$, normalization included, so the CG data come out with no $\\kappa$.\n- **$(3,2,1)$: rank 5 of 6.** One exact null vector $n(\\varepsilon)$ is present at every $\\varepsilon$, including $\\varepsilon=1/3$, with singular value $10^{-308}$ at 300 digits. At finite $\\varepsilon$ it is not HW, but as $\\varepsilon\\to0$ it tends to a vector $n_0\\in\\mathrm{HW}_{[3,2,1]}$ ($\\|P_{HW}n\\|/\\|n\\|\\to1$). So each octet eigenstate is fixed only up to $\\alpha_B n(\\varepsilon)$, and the limiting HW direction is undetermined. Fixing $\\alpha$ by minimizing the non-HW part fails: the direction error stays at 0.024 and 0.049 at both $\\varepsilon=10^{-6}$ and $10^{-9}$. The one clean functional on $\\mathrm{HW}_{[3,2,1]}$ is $C=c_{(2,1)}+hz_3c_{(1,1)}$ (11g), and $C\\cdot n_0=0$.\n- **$(2,2,2)$: rank 7 of 10.** The null vectors overlap the singlet, so its direction is trivial but its scale is not fixed (error 7.6%, same as $\\kappa_C$).\n\nBecause the null vector is exact at every $\\varepsilon$ and for every $w$, no order of the $\\varepsilon$-expansion and no choice of $w$ (including coincidences, 11f) recovers the octet mixing from $T_{(1,1)},T_{(2,1)}$ at $\\theta_1-2h$. One more independent ingredient is needed.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 12. Localizing on site 2: $t^*$ and $\\theta_2$-shifted transfer matrices\nSection 10 localizes $\\langle\\Omega|$ on site 1 at $\\theta_1-2h$; 11h shows the octet mixing and the singlet scale then stay undetermined. Here we look for transfer matrices whose action on $\\langle\\Omega|=\\langle\\Omega_{zw}\\otimes\\Omega_{zw}|$ is **site-2 local**, $\\langle\\Omega|\\mathcal O=\\langle\\Omega_{zw}|\\otimes\\langle v|$ with $v\\not\\propto\\Omega_{zw}$. All $t$'s again carry the ket's twist $\\mathrm{diag}(z)$.\n\n**Why $t^*$.** In $T=\\mathcal L^{(1)}\\mathcal L^{(2)}$ site 1 sits on the left in auxiliary space, which is why the degenerate point $\\theta_1-2h$ localizes there. The inverse monodromy $T^{-1}=\\mathcal L^{(2)-1}\\mathcal L^{(1)-1}$ puts site 2 on the left. Its transfer matrices $t^*_a$ (twist $\\mathrm{diag}(z)^{-1}$ on the left) are, up to c-number factors, ordinary $t$'s at shifted points, so the search reduces to CBR $T_\\lambda$'s at $\\theta_2+c\\,h$ and products of $t$'s there.\n\n**Locality test.** As in Section 10 a covector is an $8\\times8$ matrix $M$ (row = site 1); site-2 local means $M=\\Omega_{zw}\\,v^T$. Since $t_3$ is a c-number and $\\Omega_{zw}\\otimes\\Omega_{zw}$ is itself site-2 local, adding multiples of $t_3$ never changes locality.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* t* from the inverse monodromy: one-site Lax as a 24x24 block matrix, inverted exactly; T^-1(v) = L2^-1(v-θ2).L1^-1(v-θ1) in aux space, twist (T.Z)^-1 = Z^-1.T^-1 *)\nLaxBig[v_, s_] := ArrayFlatten[Table[KroneckerDelta[i, j] (v - thN[[s]]) IdentityMatrix[d1] + hN Ee[i, j], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]];\nblk[m_] := Table[m[[(i - 1) d1 + 1 ;; i d1, (j - 1) d1 + 1 ;; j d1]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\nLinvS[v_, s_] := LinvS[v, s] = blk[Simplify[Inverse[LaxBig[v, s]]]];\nTinvZ[v_] := TinvZ[v] = Table[Sum[(1/zN[[i]]) KroneckerProduct[IdentityMatrix[d1], LinvS[v, 2][[i, k]]] . KroneckerProduct[LinvS[v, 1][[k, j]], IdentityMatrix[d1]], {k, 3}], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\ntstar1[v_] := Sum[TinvZ[v][[i, i]], {i, 3}];\ntstar2[v_] := Sum[Sum[Signature[σ] TinvZ[v][[σ[[1]], I[[1]]]] . TinvZ[v + hN][[σ[[2]], I[[2]]]], {σ, Permutations[I]}], {I, Subsets[Range[3], {2}]}];\nvg = 3/11;\nshift1 = Select[Range[-3, 3], MatrixRank[N[{Flatten[tstar1[vg]], Flatten[tZ[[2]] /. u -> vg + # hN]}, 40]] == 1 &];\nshift2 = Select[Range[-3, 3], MatrixRank[N[{Flatten[tstar2[vg]], Flatten[tZ[[1]] /. u -> vg + # hN]}, 40]] == 1 &];\nchecks[\"t*_1(v) ∝ t_2(v+2h), t*_2(v) ∝ t_1(v+2h)\"] = shift1 === {2} && shift2 === {2};\n(* CBR scan: Ω.T_λ(u) by expanding det_{i,j} t_{λ'_j+i-j}(u+(i-1)h) over permutations, covector times matrix only *)\ntOp[0, v_] := 1; tOp[a_, v_] := If[1 <= a <= 3, tZ[[a]] /. u -> v, 0];\nconj[λ_] := Table[Count[λ, x_ /; x >= j], {j, Max[λ, 1]}];\ncovT[λ_, v_] := Module[{lc = conj[λ], n = Max[λ]}, Sum[Signature[σ] Fold[If[NumberQ[#2], #1 #2, #1 . #2] &, Ω2, Table[tOp[lc[[σ[[i]]]] + i - σ[[i]], v + (i - 1) hN], {i, n}]], {σ, Permutations[Range[n]]}]];\nasMat[c_] := Partition[c, d1];\nsite1Q[c_] := zeroQ[asMat[c] - Outer[Times, asMat[c] . Ω1/(Ω1 . Ω1), Ω1]];\nsite2Q[c_] := zeroQ[Transpose[asMat[c]] - Outer[Times, Transpose[asMat[c]] . Ω1/(Ω1 . Ω1), Ω1]];\nclassify[c_] := Which[zeroQ[c], \"0\", zeroQ[c - (c . Ω2/(Ω2 . Ω2)) Ω2], \"eig\", site2Q[c], \"SITE 2\", site1Q[c], \"site 1\", True, \"·\"];\nshapes = {{1}, {2}, {3}, {1, 1}, {2, 1}, {3, 1}, {2, 2}, {3, 2}, {3, 3}};\n{scanTime, {scan2, scan1}} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[classify[covT[λ, thN[[s]] + cc hN]], {s, {2, 1}}, {λ, shapes}, {cc, -5, 5}]];\nchecks[\"CBR scan at θ2+ch (c=-5..5): only T_(1,1)(θ2+h) is site-2 local\"] = Position[scan2, \"SITE 2\"] === {{4, 7}};\nchecks[\"CBR scan at θ1+ch: site-1 local = T_(1,1)(θ1-2h), T_(2,1)(θ1-2h) only\"] = Sort[Position[scan1, \"site 1\"]] === {{4, 4}, {5, 4}};\nGrid[Join[{{\"t*_1(v) ∝ t_2(v+s h), s =\", shift1, \"t*_2(v) ∝ t_1(v+s h), s =\", shift2}},\n   {Join[{\"λ \\\\ u =\"}, Table[\"θ2\" <> If[cc == 0, \"\", ToString[cc] <> \"h\"], {cc, -5, 5}]]}, Table[Join[{shapes[[k]]}, scan2[[k]]], {k, Length[shapes]}],\n   {Join[{\"λ \\\\ u =\"}, Table[\"θ1\" <> If[cc == 0, \"\", ToString[cc] <> \"h\"], {cc, -5, 5}]]}, Table[Join[{shapes[[k]]}, scan1[[k]]], {k, Length[shapes]}], {{\"scan time (s)\", scanTime}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Center]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
