n></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.155em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:4.81em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.155em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.655em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.655em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.655em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.655em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.31em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.655em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.155em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[895]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{site-2 local products \\{a,x,b,y\\}} & \\begin{pmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 1\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{<$\\Omega$|t2($\\theta$2+h) factorizes, f = ($\\theta$12-h)($\\theta$12-3h)} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{<$\\Omega$|t2($\\theta$2+h)t1($\\theta$2-h) factorizes, $\\alpha$ = -($\\theta$12-h)\\^{}2($\\theta$12-3h), $\\beta$ = 6h\\^{}4 $\\chi$3 ($\\theta$12-h)($\\theta$12-3h)} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{nontrivial (rank 3)} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "ddb15509-0388-4e97-809b-17a486c5046c"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result 12 (exact, numeric point P1).**\n- **$t^*$.** $t^*_1(v)\\propto t_2(v+2h)$ and $t^*_2(v)\\propto t_1(v+2h)$, so the $t^*$'s are ordinary $t$'s at shifted points; the scan over $T_\\lambda$ and products at $\\theta_2+\\mathbb Z h$ therefore covers them.\n- **CBR scan, $u=\\theta_2+ch$, $c=-5..5$, all $\\lambda\\subseteq3\\times3$ with $\\lambda_3=0$:** the only site-2 local one is $T_{(1,1)}(\\theta_2+h)=t_2(\\theta_2+h)\\propto t^*_1(\\theta_2-h)$. No $T_{(2,1)}$ localizes on site 2 at any integer shift. At $\\theta_1+ch$ the same scan returns exactly the Section 10 pair $T_{(1,1)},T_{(2,1)}$ at $\\theta_1-2h$.\n- **Products of two $t$'s at $\\theta_2+\\mathbb Zh$:** the only new site-2 local one is $t_2(\\theta_2+h)\\,t_1(\\theta_2-h)\\propto t^*_1(\\theta_2-h)\\,t^*_2(\\theta_2-3h)$. This is the site-2 analogue of $T_{(2,1)}(\\theta_1-2h)=t_2(\\theta_1-2h)t_1(\\theta_1-h)-t_3$, but the gap between the two arguments is $-2h$, not $+h$, so it is not a CBR-fused $T^*_{(2,1)}$.\n- **Factorization against the one-site chain at $\\theta_2$** (same twist):\n$$\\langle\\Omega|t_2(\\theta_2+h)=(\\theta_{12}-h)(\\theta_{12}-3h)\\;\\langle\\Omega_{zw}|\\otimes\\langle\\Omega_{zw}|t^{L=1,\\theta_2}_2(\\theta_2+h),$$\n$$\\langle\\Omega|t_2(\\theta_2+h)t_1(\\theta_2-h)=\\langle\\Omega_{zw}|\\otimes\\Big[-(\\theta_{12}-h)^2(\\theta_{12}-3h)\\,\\langle\\Omega_{zw}|t^{L=1}_2(\\theta_2+h)t^{L=1}_1(\\theta_2-h)+3h^3\\chi_3(\\theta_{12}-h)(\\theta_{12}-3h)\\,\\langle\\Omega_{zw}|\\Big].$$\n  The site-1 factor of the first is the same $f_{(1,1)}$ as in Section 10. All coefficients were **fitted at one point** ($h=1/2$, $\\theta_{12}=31/35$, $\\chi_3=5/4$). Note $3h^3\\chi_3$ is the one-site qdet at $\\theta_2-h$. The three vectors $\\Omega_{zw}$, $v_A$, $v_B$ are independent.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 12b. Undoing $R$ on site 2 and the highest-weight reach (finite twist)\nAs in 10b–10c, with the roles of the sites swapped: the covector is $c=e_1^T\\otimes\\langle w|R^{-1}$ for the site-2 one-site vectors $w_A=\\Omega_{zw}t^{L=1}_2(\\theta_2+h)$ and $w_B=w_A\\,t^{L=1}_1(\\theta_2-h)$. The cell tests the 10b identity at $\\theta_2$, $\\langle w|R^{-1}=e_1^T\\,T^{L=1,\\theta_2}[g^{-T}\\mathrm{diag}(z)g^T]$, and lists the norm of the projection of $c$ onto each $\\mathrm{HW}_\\mu$, next to the site-1 covectors of 10c.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* one-site chain at site s with an arbitrary 3x3 twist M on the right *)\noneT[s_, M_][v_] := Table[Sum[(KroneckerDelta[i, l] (v - thN[[s]]) IdentityMatrix[d1] + hN Ee[i, l]) M[[l, k]], {l, 3}], {i, 3}, {k, 3}];\nonet[s_, M_, a_, v_] := Sum[Sum[Signature[σ] Dot @@ Table[oneT[s, M][v - (k - 1) hN][[σ[[k]], I[[k]]]], {k, a}], {σ, Permutations[I]}], {I, Subsets[Range[3], {a}]}];\nRgInv = MatrixExp[-(r3 /. rOm) Ee[2, 3]] . MatrixExp[-(r2 /. rOm) Ee[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[-(r1 /. rOm) Ee[1, 2]];\ngF = MatrixExp[(r1 /. rOm) ee[1, 2]] . MatrixExp[(r2 /. rOm) ee[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[(r3 /. rOm) ee[2, 3]];\nZconj = Inverse[Transpose[gF]] . DiagonalMatrix[zN] . Transpose[gF];\n(* the four one-site covectors: site 1 at θ1-2h (Section 10) and site 2 at θ2+h, θ2-h *)\nZd1 = DiagonalMatrix[zN]; u1 = thN[[1]] - 2 hN; u2 = thN[[2]] + hN;\nw1s[\"11\"] = Ω1 . onet[1, Zd1, 2, u1]; w1s[\"21\"] = w1s[\"11\"] . onet[1, Zd1, 1, u1 + hN] - Ω1 . onet[1, Zd1, 3, u1 + hN];\nw2s[\"A\"] = Ω1 . onet[2, Zd1, 2, u2]; w2s[\"B\"] = w2s[\"A\"] . onet[2, Zd1, 1, thN[[2]] - hN];\nchecks[\"site-2 one-site vectors match 12 (w_A, w_B)\"] = zeroQ[w2s[\"A\"] - wA] && zeroQ[w2s[\"B\"] - wB];\nchecks[\"<w_A|R^-1 = e1^T t2^{L=1,θ2}[g^-T z g^T](θ2+h)\"] = zeroQ[w2s[\"A\"] . RgInv - UnitVector[d1, 1] . onet[2, Zconj, 2, u2]];\nchecks[\"<w_B|R^-1 = e1^T (t2 t1)^{L=1,θ2}[g^-T z g^T]\"] = zeroQ[w2s[\"B\"] . RgInv - UnitVector[d1, 1] . onet[2, Zconj, 2, u2] . onet[2, Zconj, 1, thN[[2]] - hN]];\ne1v = UnitVector[d1, 1];\nhwCov = <|\"site1 (1,1)\" -> Flatten[KroneckerProduct[w1s[\"11\"] . RgInv, e1v]], \"site1 (2,1)\" -> Flatten[KroneckerProduct[w1s[\"21\"] . RgInv, e1v]],\n   \"site2 A\" -> Flatten[KroneckerProduct[e1v, w2s[\"A\"] . RgInv]], \"site2 B\" -> Flatten[KroneckerProduct[e1v, w2s[\"B\"] . RgInv]]|>;\n(* hwB (Section 11) is numeric; RootReduce first, since surd sums that cancel to 0 make N[] hit meprec *)\nhwProj[c_, μ_] := hwB[μ] . N[RootReduce /@ c, 60];\nrk321 = MatrixRank[Table[hwProj[c, {3, 2, 1}], {c, Values[hwCov]}], Tolerance -> 10^-20];\nchecks[\"[3,2,1] HW projections of {site1 (1,1), site1 (2,1), site2 A, site2 B} span both copies (rank 2)\"] = rk321 == 2;\nGrid[Join[{Join[{\"μ  (|projection onto HW_μ|)\"}, Keys[hwCov]]}, Table[Join[{μ}, Table[With[{p = hwProj[c, μ]}, If[Norm[p] < 10^-25, 0, N[Norm[p], 5]]], {c, Values[hwCov]}]], {μ, hwSecs}],\n   {{\"identity at θ2 (A, B)\", checks[\"<w_A|R^-1 = e1^T t2^{L=1,θ2}[g^-T z g^T](θ2+h)\"], checks[\"<w_B|R^-1 = e1^T (t2 t1)^{L=1,θ2}[g^-T z g^T]\"], \"[3,2,1] rank\", rk321}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"758596\" data-output-id=\"257\" data-out-n=\"2451\" data-sub-idx=\"19\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"83\" data-sub-start=\"20\" data-sub-end=\"21\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[2451]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:8.44em;vertical-align:-3.95em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.49em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.45em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:8.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-3.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">μ</span><span class=\"mord\"> (|projection onto HW_</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">μ</span><span class=\"mord\">|)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-5.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\