      {
       "data": "Out[2434]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{site-2 locality at $\\varepsilon$=1/3 (max rel. resid)} & \\text{0.}\\times 10^{\\text{-74}} &  &  &  &  &  & \\\\\\hline\\mu  & \\text{dim} & \\text{site1} & \\text{site1+$\\Omega$} & \\text{site2} & \\text{site2+$\\Omega$} & \\text{site1+site2} & \\text{site1+site2+$\\Omega$}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{4,2,0\\right\\} & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\\\\\hline\\left\\{4,1,1\\right\\} & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,3,0\\right\\} & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,2,1\\right\\} & 6 & 5 & 6 & 5 & 6 & 6 & 6\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2,2\\right\\} & 10 & 7 & 9 & 7 & 9 & 10 & 10\\\\\\hline\\text{time (s)} & 0.7343 &  &  &  &  &  & \\\\\\hline\\varepsilon  & \\mu  & \\text{dim} & \\text{rank site1+site2 (+x0)} & \\text{rel. error $\\Psi$} & \\text{rel. error HW part} &  & \\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000} & \\left\\{4,2,0\\right\\} & 1 & 1 & 0 & 0 &  & \\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000} & \\left\\{4,1,1\\right\\} & 2 & 2 & 0 & 0 &  & \\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000} & \\left\\{3,3,0\\right\\} & 2 & 2 & 0 & 0 &  & \\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000} & \\left\\{3,2,1\\right\\} & 6 & 6 & 0 & 0 &  & \\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000} & \\left\\{3,2,1\\right\\} & 6 & 6 & 0 & 0 &  & \\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{1000000} & \\left\\{2,2,2\\right\\} & 10 & 10 & 8.27\\times 10^{-123… [latex truncated: 1725 chars total]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "d82a76c7-268f-4598-9896-699466e2c230"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result 12b–12c.**\n- **Undoing $R$ on site 2 (12b, exact at P1).** The 10b identity holds at $\\theta_2$: $\\langle w|R^{-1}=e_1^T\\,T^{L=1,\\theta_2}[g^{-T}\\mathrm{diag}(z)g^T]$ for both $w_A$ and $w_B$.\n- **HW reach at finite twist.** $e_1^T\\otimes w_AR^{-1}$ reaches $[4,2,0]$, $[4,1,1]$ and $[3,2,1]$, but not $[3,3,0]$ or the singlet. This is the mirror of site-1 $(1,1)$, which misses $[4,1,1]$ and the singlet. $e_1^T\\otimes w_BR^{-1}$ reaches every irrep.\n- **Locality at other twists.** At $\\varepsilon=1/3$, for 12 random $w$, the two-site covectors $\\langle\\Omega|t_2(\\theta_2+h)$ and $\\langle\\Omega|t_2(\\theta_2+h)t_1(\\theta_2-h)$ are site-2 local to $10^{-74}$ (80 digits).\n- **Rank per weight space, with $x_0$** ($\\varepsilon=1/3$, 12 values of $w$):\n\n| sector | dim | site1 (= 11h) | site1+Ω | site2 | site2+Ω | **site1+site2** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [4,2,0] | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 |\n| [4,1,1], [3,3,0] | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 |\n| (3,2,1) | 6 | 5 | 6 | 5 | 6 | **6** |\n| (2,2,2) | 10 | 7 | 9 | 7 | 9 | **10** |\n\n- **Reconstruction.** With site1 + site2 (and $\\langle x_0|\\Psi\\rangle=1$), all six HW-limit states are reconstructed **exactly**, including both octets and the singlet scale. The relative error in $\\Psi_B$ and in its HW part is 0 for every state except the singlet, where it is $8\\times10^{-123}$ ($\\varepsilon=10^{-6}$) and $2\\times10^{-77}$ ($\\varepsilon=10^{-9}$). So the 11h null vector $n(\\varepsilon)$ is lifted, and the octet mixing is fixed with no $\\kappa$.\n- **Side remark.** 11h never used the bare overlap $\\langle\\Omega(w)|\\Psi\\rangle$ as a row. Adding it to the site-1 family alone already fixes the octet (rank 6), but not the singlet (9 of 10). Site 2 is needed for the singlet scale.\n\n**Audit update (Section 13).** The site-2 scalar coefficient is corrected to $6h^4\\chi_3f$ and all four localization identities are now proved symbolically. The full determinant-Q-to-reconstruction chain passes at two chain points with only three bra twists.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary of checks\nBoolean checks must be `True`. Numeric checks are residuals and must be below $10^{-25}$; the \"not a zero test\" entries are sizes and must be large.\n\n**Expected FAILs.** These rows are records of what does *not* work, not bugs:\n- the two R_B and row-choice checks from the single combined bracket (Section 6);\n- the per-ladder \"pair-choice\" check: the pairs $\\{(1,3),(2,1),(3,2)\\}$ are not equivalent to the L=1 pairs $\\{(1,3),(1,2),(2,3)\\}$.\n\n**Main result (Sections 7–9).** In the diagonal frame, for all 64 eigenstates of the twist-$z$ chain,\n$$\\Omega^{(2)}\\cdot\\Psi_B=\\frac{\\Omega^{(2)}\\cdot y_0^{(2)}}{c_0\\,\\langle x_0|y_0\\rangle^2\\,\\Phi_Q^{\\rm vac}(y_0)}\\;\\frac{\\det N[B,\\mathrm{vac}]}{\\Psi_Q^B(x_0)}\\;\\langle x_0^{(2)}|\\Psi_B\\rangle .$$\nIt holds to 50 digits. The ingredients:\n- $x_0^{(2)}$, $y_0^{(2)}$, $\\Psi_Q$ and $\\Phi_Q$ are products over sites;\n- $\\langle x_0|y_0\\rangle^2=(9h^4)^2$;\n- $\\det N$ has rows $(i,j;k)$ for $(i,j)\\in\\{(1,3),(1,2),(2,3)\\}$ and columns of type $\\times\\,x^{\\beta-1}$.\n\n**Preferred brackets (Section 9).** Both brackets go around all poles, with insertions $1$ and $e^{2\\pi iu/h}$. Then\n$$c_0=\\frac{(\\varepsilon_1-\\varepsilon_2)^3}{16h^{12}\\,\\theta_{12}^3(\\theta_{12}^2-h^2)^4(\\theta_{12}^2-4h^2)^2},\\qquad \\varepsilon_s=e^{2\\pi i\\theta_s/h},\\quad \\theta_{12}=\\theta_1-\\theta_2.$$\nThis is $(\\varepsilon_2-\\varepsilon_1)^3$ times the per-ladder $c_0$ of Section 7, as expected from the row mixing, and it was confirmed by direct computation.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "passQ[k_, v_] := Which[v === True, True, v === False, False, StringContainsQ[k, \"not a zero test\"], v > 10^-20, StringContainsQ[k, \"min gap\"], v > 10^-10, NumericQ[v], v < 10^-25, True, False];\nGrid[Prepend[KeyValueMap[{#1, If[NumericQ[#2], ScientificForm[N[#2, 3], 3], #2], If[passQ[#1, #2], Style[\"PASS\", Darker[Green]], Style[\"FAIL\", Red]]} &, checks], {\"check\", \"value\", \"\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
