  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 13e. Exact site-2 highest-weight overlaps and the minimum number of bra twists\n\nThe table uses the exact orthonormal HW basis returned by the two raising-operator null spaces. The auxiliary twist is $Z'=g^{-T}\\operatorname{diag}(z)g^T=\\left(\\begin{smallmatrix}z_a&0&0\\\\a&z_b&0\\\\b&c&z_c\\end{smallmatrix}\\right)$. Entries are the **one-site** site-2 rows after undoing the rotation; they do not include spectator factors. These are covector overlaps, not permission to discard finite-twist corrections to the eigenstate.\n\nFor the four operator rows and one $x_0$ normalization, two bra twists give at most nine equations in the ten-dimensional $(2,2,2)$ weight space. Three are therefore necessary for unrestricted finite-twist reconstruction. An exact rank calculation below proves they suffice generically.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "auditSite2HW=Table[With[{sec=Flatten[Position[wtBasis,mu]],hb=auditHW[mu]},\n{mu,Factor[hh^2 Flatten[Outer[Times,auditSeed,auditSymVA]][[sec]] . Transpose[hb]],Factor[hh^3 Flatten[Outer[Times,auditSeed,auditSymVB]][[sec]] . Transpose[hb]]}],{mu,auditHWSectors}];\nauditExactRows=Append[Flatten[Table[auditRows[zN,ww,hN,thN],{ww,Take[auditWList,3]}],1],auditX0[zN]];\nauditExactRanks=Table[With[{sec=Flatten[Position[wtBasis,mu]]},{mu,Length[sec],MatrixRank[RootReduce[auditExactRows[[All,sec]]]]}],{mu,auditHWSectors}];\nGrid[Join[{{\"mu\",\"site2 A HW components\",\"site2 B HW components\"}},auditSite2HW,{{\"mu\",\"weight dimension\",\"exact rank with 3 w + x0\"}},auditExactRanks],Frame->All,Alignment->Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
